ed rectangle which is the operational  database side  and this is a very common architectural  pattern which we have seen  where spanner connects with gke and  so it can seamlessly scale both uh from  the  client side as well as on the database  side so it's a very typical  uh pattern and then as i was mentioning  earlier it's extremely important that  the database can hook up with the legacy  systems or  other systems which are there for  example the other core banking systems  which are there or payment gateways as  shown at the bottom and then as the data  is getting updated in the  oltp database which is spanner  the data almost in near real time is  getting  populated in analytics and warehousing  solutions as well  so the customer is able to do their olap  queries and generate insights on that  that is within  bigquery and cloud ai data catalog and  everything so  that whole chain is set up  using pub sub and data flow and on the  security and governance size we  offer all kinds of integration like  cloud monitoring dlp  and customers are able to benefit  with that across the board so this is  just one of those  solution architectures where spanner  plays that operational database role and  is able to seamlessly scale along with  the rest of the architecture  which is extremely critical for our  customers next  uh this is i'm not talking about the  complete  retail omnichannel retail architecture  for this customer  but just focusing on the spanner piece  so in this case the use case was  the omni-channel retail customer is  getting updated prices delivered to gcp  through an external system both as a  streaming data pipeline  as well as in batches the data was being  uploaded  and then spanner was the database of  record for  all the skews with the updated prices  and then spanner  is serving those prices to all the  applications which  this omni-channel retailer is running so  as you can see from the solution  architecture  that the prices are are being uploaded  in cloud storage  and uh then through uh load service  running as part of kubernetes is being  uploaded into  cloud spanner and then cloud spanner is  just  serving all the requests from the  pricing api standpoint  again in this case spanner is getting a  lot of  right load as well as read load and  depending on  the traffic it's able to scale up based  on the needs  of the application and the time of the  day and everything  so again very important and in this case  they were using a multi-regional  instance so  five nines of availability with global  presence and everything  so uh extremely happy with the way it  turned out and custom  and the customer is really uh very happy  with the solution  so switching gears now let's talk about  what's new in cloud spanner  uh and uh and just  a reflection of the past a little bit so  we had a busy 2019 we delivered  capabilities  and three of in in all areas basically  we have categorized in these three major  areas enterprise  capabilities developer productivity and  sql so on the enterprise side  i already talked about vpc access  transparency which is  extremely critical for some of our  regulatory  industry users where when even a google  srd when they touched your data for any  reason  that that kind of an action has to be  locked  so that is access transparency spanner  is uh  supports access transparency and we  updated our sla in september 2019.  basically now all your cloud spanner  instances  uh even with a single node are covered  under the same production sla  so this way uh even for smaller  workloads  you are protected by the same sla which  which we offer  before september 2019 it we used to  require minimum three nodes in an  instance  and the reason we were able to update  our sla is because spanner behind the  scenes is replicated  so even in case of a regional instance  there are three replicas  and we are able to offer you that high  availability uh with a single node  and multi-region x multiple  replicas like five seven and nine  replica configurations is something  which we offer today  on the developer productivity size we  continue to invest in orms  we have launched a new initiative uh and  something which is getting a lot of  momentum called as cloud spanner  ecosystem  uh the website is actually cloud spanner  ecosystem.dev or dev  and because as you noticed we have a lot  of momentum spanner  a number of our customers are  contributing tools  uh in the ecosystem for other spanner  users  and we have a lot of partners  contributing  tools and googlers as well so we created  this ecosystem  as a single place where they can make  their contributions for the benefit of  the overall community and we are seeing  a lot of fraction  please check it out there are a number  of tools which are available  for our users and last but not the least  on the sql side we continue to innovate  for the query optimizer we launched cost  based index selection as part of the  query optimizer optimization we have  html support we launch with clause again  trying to  offer all the capabilities which you  expect from  a database from the sql site  we had a fairly busy 2020 so far  again in those all those three areas we  continue to make  improvements and launch new capabilities  uh  and like manage backup restore i'm not  going to spend too much time here i'll  go into details later  we continue to expand on our  multi-regional configuration options  uh we now we originally had four  multi-regional conf instance  configurations  we recently launched two new  multi-regional  uh configurations one an asia only multi  region and another one in europe  and uh then we recently launched uh a  change watcher solution which is not a  native capability but a solution  which is built on top of uh spanner uh  leveraging the commit timestamp feature  where  customers can watch out for changes  which are happening within the database  and on the developer productivity side  we  emulator is something this is a offline  emulator i'm going to talk more in  details later  but c plus plus client library  transaction statistics  and harbor bridge which is another tool  which we  which was recently contributed in cloud  spanner ecosystem  it is a it is to aid in  migration uh it actually the capability  it provides is  if a customer has a postgresql uh  schema and they use harbour bridge the  tool can recommend an equivalent  spamming schema with it  uh so originally we launched it for  postgres sql support  and with for my sequel we have launched  it in beta  right now and on sql side query  optimizer versioning i'll talk more in  details on that  later and foreign keys so i'm not going  to go into details of each one of these  cable  capabilities but i'll pick one from each  of these areas  and tell you a little bit more about  them  so first and foremost is manage backups  uh which  we launched for with general  availability  in april uh so this is on demand managed  backups  uh this is primarily to offer protection  to our customers against operator  application errors which can cause  logical data corruption  so what we offer is consistent backup  for regional and multi-regional  instances and uh what we are optimizing  for  is uh extremely fast restores our first  time to first by taxes so because if  you run into an issue you would like to  get back online with your application as  soon as possible and we recognize that  so uh even for a backups which is  terabytes of  uh in size you can expect to get first  bet access as part of your restore  process  within minutes so that is something  which we have really optimized for  uh you can restore from your backup  within the same instance configuration  or basically within the same instance or  another instance within the same  instance configuration  and the maximum retention time for  backups is one year  and we from a security perspective we  uh our im access permissions are  separate for backup so  customers have the flexibility to create  a separate role  just to manage the backups and do the  risk tools  so that is there and again the feature  is available through api console gcloud  local emulator so this is something  which we  announced in beta in march  i'm happy to announce the general  availability of local emulator  as part of this uh talk so this is now  generally available we have  uh implemented a lot more capabilities  as part of this general available launch  for local emulator  it is an offline open source local  emulator the code is open  you can take a look it's in a github  repository  it offers complete rest and gp and grpc  api support  and it offers sql basically dml  and ddl support most importantly it has  complete support for information schema  as well  now all client libraries are supported  for working with emulator  and this really we have got great  feedback from a number of our customers  and  it has really helped them from our  productivity developer productivity  perspective  because now they can and do a very quick  correctness testing for their  application in an offline environment  and last but not the least uh cloud  spanner  offered query optimizer versioning  capability to our customers  uh and this is a ga feature so basically  what does it mean  now users have the flexibility to run  their queries with a  specific version of query optimizer  there's a  range of choices which we offer you can  pin your complete database  on a query optimizer version or you can  you can decide to pin just your  application on  a specific query optimizer version with  the default  query optimizer for the database as  being something different so you can  override  the default on the database and finally  you can use a specific query optimizer  version as a query hint as well  and you can test your query with a  specific query optimized version  so there's a range of choices and  flexibility which we offer as part of  this feature  and c